    <briefdescription>
<para>Set of one or more 2D primitives. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1VertexArray" kindref="compound">sf::VertexArray</ref></computeroutput> is a very simple wrapper around a dynamic array of vertices and a primitives type.</para>
<para>It inherits <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Drawable" kindref="compound">sf::Drawable</ref></computeroutput>, but unlike other drawables it is not transformable.</para>
<para>Example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">sf::VertexArray<sp/>lines(<ref refid="group__graphics_1gga5ee56ac1339984909610713096283b1bae7f9e73b8edd21f420a63b3ace5768a2" kindref="member">sf::PrimitiveType::LineStrip</ref>,<sp/>4);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">lines[0].position<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacesf_1af14b40e82368dd601a7ef8037214804d" kindref="member">sf::Vector2f</ref>(10,<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">lines[1].position<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacesf_1af14b40e82368dd601a7ef8037214804d" kindref="member">sf::Vector2f</ref>(20,<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">lines[2].position<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacesf_1af14b40e82368dd601a7ef8037214804d" kindref="member">sf::Vector2f</ref>(30,<sp/>5);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">lines[3].position<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacesf_1af14b40e82368dd601a7ef8037214804d" kindref="member">sf::Vector2f</ref>(40,<sp/>2);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">window.draw(lines);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="structsf_1_1Vertex" kindref="compound">sf::Vertex</ref></computeroutput> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
